<title>USA: AirNet Systems Inc Q2 net rises.</title>
<headline>AirNet Systems Inc Q2 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>COLUMBUS, Ohio 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Unaudited - in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>			     Three months ended    Six months ended</p>
<p>				     March 31,	     March 31,</p>
<p>			     1997     1996		1997     1996</p>
<p>				    restated		     restated</p>
<p> Net revenues	  $22,235 $19,209	   $43,026  $37,606</p>
<p> Net income		3,093   1,868	     5,578    3,687</p>
<p>Pro forma net</p>
<p>  income			--   2,081		  --    4,063</p>
<p> Earnings per share     0.25	--		0.44	 --</p>
<p>Pro forma earnings</p>
<p>  per share		   --    0.24		  --     0.48</p>
<p>Adjusted pro forma</p>
<p>  earnings per share     --    0.17		  --     0.33</p>
<p>Weighted average common</p>
<p>  shares outstanding  12,621   8,507	    12,601    8,507</p>
<p> EBITDA		    31.8%   31.2%	     31.7%    31.4%</p>
<p> EBIT			23.2%   20.0%	     21.7%    20.0%</p>
<p>NOTE: All balances have been restated to reflect ECC's results of operations under the pooling of interests method of accounting.  </p>
<p>Prior to the company's initial public offering on May 31, 1996, it operated as an S Corporation under the Internal Revenue Code for tax purposes and so only earnings related to Express Convenience Center Inc, purchased in January 1997 and accounted for under the pooling of interests method of accounting, were subject to income taxes.</p>
<p>1995 balances include pro forma adjustments incurred as a result of the IPO.</p>
<p>The adjusted pro forma earnings per share assumes the shares issued in the IPO were outstanding for the six months ended March 31, 1996, for a pro forma balance of shares outstanding of 12,463,788.</p>
<p>((--New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
